Test fonts of the label crate
=============================

The dejavu-sans-*.ttf files are subsets of
DejaVu Sans 2.37 (DejaVuSans.ttf), made with fontTools 4.55.3 (`fontTools.subset`, hinting and
the layout tables dropped). They are modified versions of the Font Software under the licence
below, whose names contain neither "Bitstream", "Vera", nor "Arev":

- dejavu-sans-subset.ttf: printable ASCII and U+00ED; the left side bearing of `l` is lowered
  from 193 to 93, so that it differs from the glyph's xMin, for the tests of ADR-0028.
- dejavu-sans-digits.ttf: the digits and the space; it has no `?`.
- dejavu-sans-symbol.ttf: the digits and the space, with only a Windows Symbol character map.
- dejavu-sans-both.ttf: dejavu-sans-digits.ttf with a Windows Symbol map that maps each digit to
  the next one and a Windows Unicode map that maps `9` to glyph 500, past the font's glyphs.
- dejavu-sans-mac.ttf: dejavu-sans-digits.ttf with only an Apple Roman character map.
- dejavu-sans-broken.ttf: dejavu-sans-digits.ttf whose `1` and glyph 0 are replaced by a glyph
  that names 1000 points and holds none.
- dejavu-sans-huge.ttf: dejavu-sans-digits.ttf with 16 units per em, and its `1` and the
  advance of `1` 20 times as large, so that the glyph can reach millions of pixels.

boxes-cff.otf is drawn for these tests with fontTools' FontBuilder: a box for each digit, in CFF
outlines; it carries no third-party work and stands under the repository's licence.

The licence of DejaVu Sans, as its name table records it:

Fonts are (c) Bitstream (see below). DejaVu changes are in public domain. Glyphs imported from Arev fonts are (c) Tavmjung Bah (see below)

